<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21246] quota: usage is lost when an ID becomes enforced by default quota</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21246</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When default quotas are applied, newly enforced QIDs at the quota slaves(OSTs and MDTs) don't report quota usage to the QMT.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This happens when:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;a default limit is set ("lfs setquota -U/-G/-P -B ...") while the ID already uses the default quota, or&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;an ID is switched back to the default quota ("lfs setquota -u ID -D") while a default limit is set.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The usage stays unknown until the ID writes again to the same target or the quota slave reintegrates, so it is most visible with files spread over several OSTs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example (2 OSTs, default limit 10 MB):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the user writes 20 MB to OST0000 while no default limit is set&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;"lfs setquota -U -B 10M" is set&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the user can still write to OST0001 because OST0000 didn't report 20MB usage. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
